ey, this query will show a hard loading state and make a network request to fetch the data."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the network request has completed, the returned data will be cached under the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"['todos']"},{"type":"text","value":" key."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The data will be marked as stale after the configured "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"staleTime"},{"type":"text","value":" (defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":", or immediately)."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A second instance of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: fetchTodos })"},{"type":"text","value":" mounts elsewhere."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Since the cache already has data for the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"['todos']"},{"type":"text","value":" key from the first query, that data is immediately returned from the cache."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The new instance triggers a new network request using its query function."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note that regardless of whether both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchTodos"},{"type":"text","value":" query functions are identical or not, both queries' "},{"type":"link","href":"../reference/functions/useQuery.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"}]},{"type":"text","value":" are updated (including "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isFetching"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isPending"},{"type":"text","value":", and other related values) because they have the same query key."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the request completes successfully, the cache's data under the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"['todos']"},{"type":"text","value":" key is updated with the new data, and both instances are updated with the new data."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both instances of the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: fetchTodos })"},{"type":"text","value":" query are unmounted and no longer in use."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Since there are no more active instances of this query, a garbage collection timeout is set using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gcTime"},{"type":"text","value":" to delete and garbage collect the query (defaults to "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5 minutes"}]},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before the cache timeout (gcTime) has completed, another instance of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: fetchTodos })"},{"type":"text","value":" mounts. The query immediately returns the available cached data while the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchTodos"},{"type":"text","value":" function is being run in the background. When it completes successfully, it will populate the cache with fresh data."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The final instance of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: fetchTodos })"},{"type":"text","value":" unmounts."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No more instances of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: fetchTodos })"},{"type":"text","value":" appear within "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5 minutes"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The cached data under the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"['todos']"},{"type":"text","value":" key is deleted and garbage collected."}]}]}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"basic-example","text":"Basic Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n> Please thoroughly read the [Important Defaults](./important-defaults.md) before reading this guide\n\n## Basic Example\n\nThis caching example illustrates the story and lifecycle of:\n\n- Query Instances with and without cache data\n- Background Refetching\n- Inactive Queries\n- Garbage Collection\n\nLet's assume we are using the default `gcTime` of **5 minutes** and the default `staleTime` of `0`.\n\n- A new instance of `useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: fetchTodos })` mounts.\n  - Since no other queries have been made with the `['todos']` query key, this query will show a hard loading state and make a network request to fetch the data.\n  - When the network request has completed, the returned data will be cached under the `['todos']` key.\n  - The data will be marked as stale after the configured `staleTime` (defaults to `0`, or immediately).\n- A second instance of `useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: fetchTodos })` mounts elsewhere.\n  - Since the cache already has data for the `['todos']` key from the first query, that data is immediately returned from the cache.\n  - The new instance triggers a new network request using its query function.\n    - Note that regardless of whether both `fetchTodos` query functions are identical or not, both queries' [`status`](../reference/functions/useQuery.md) are updated (including `isFetching`, `isPending`, and other related values) because they have the same query key.\n  - When the request completes successfully, the cache's data under the `['todos']` key is updated with the new data, and both instances are updated with the new data.\n- Both instances of the `useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: fetchTodos })` query are unmounted and no longer in use.\n  - Since there are no more active instances of this query, a garbage collection timeout is set using `gcTime` to delete and garbage collect the query (defaults to **5 minutes**).\n- Before the cache timeout (gcTime) has completed, another instance of `useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: fetchTodos })` mounts. The query immediately returns the available cached data while the `fetchTodos` function is being run in the background. When it completes successfully, it will populate the cache with fresh data.\n- The final instance of `useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: fetchTodos })` unmounts.\n- No more instances of `useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: fetchTodos })` appear within **5 minutes**.\n  - The cached data under the `['todos']` key is deleted and garbage collected.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: caching\ntitle: Caching Examples\n---\n\n> Please thoroughly read the [Important Defaults](./important-defaults.md) before reading this guide\n\n## Basic Example\n\nThis caching example illustrates the story and lifecycle of:\n\n- Query Instances with and without cache data\n- Background Refetching\n- Inactive Queries\n- Garbage Collection\n\nLet's assume we are using the default `gcTime` of **5 minutes** and the default `staleTime` of `0`.\n\n- A new instance of `useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: fetchTodos })` mounts.\n  - Since no other queries have been made with the `['todos']` query key, this query will show a hard loading state and make a network request to fetch the data.\n  - When the network request has completed, the returned data will be cached under the `['todos']` key.\n  - The data will be marked as stale after the configured `staleTime` (defaults to `0`, or immediately).\n- A second instance of `useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: fetchTodos })` mounts elsewhere.\n  - Since the cache already has data for the `['todos']` key from the first query, that data is immediately returned from the cache.\n  - The new instance triggers a new network request using its query function.\n    - Note that regardless of whether both `fetchTodos` query functions are identical or not, both queries' [`status`](../reference/functions/useQuery.md) are updated (including `isFetching`, `isPending`, and other related values) because they have the same query key.\n  - When the request completes successfully, the cache's data under the `['todos']` key is updated with the new data, and both instances are updated with the new data.\n- Both instances of the `useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: fetchTodos })` query are unmounted and no longer in use.\n  - Since there are no more active instances of this query, a garbage collection timeout is set using `gcTime` to delete and garbage collect the query (defaults to **5 minutes**).\n- Before the cache timeout (gcTime) has completed, another instance of `useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: fetchTodos })` mounts. The query immediately returns the available cached data while the `fetchTodos` function is being run in the background. When it completes successfully, it will populate the cache with fresh data.\n- The final instance of `useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: fetchTodos })` unmounts.\n- No more instances of `useQuery({ queryKey: ['todos'], queryFn: fetchTodos })` appear within **5 minutes**.\n  - The cached data under the `['todos']` key is deleted and garbage collected.\n"}
